<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01256#trivialization_of_medical_procedure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#BackgroundKnowledge> .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01256#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a close-up of a black and white Boston Terrier dog with a sad, tearful expression. The text overlay reads: 'when your debit card decline at the abortion clinic and they have to put the baby back in.' The overall intent is to create dark humor by juxtaposing the dog's pitiful expression with a highly sensitive and distressing scenario involving financial failure at a reproductive health clinic, which then leads to a grotesque and absurd consequence. This meme is harmful as it trivializes a serious medical and personal situation, potentially causing distress to individuals who have experienced abortion-related financial difficulties or who are sensitive to reproductive health issues. The humor is derived from the absurdity of the situation and the dog's emotive face, which serves as a visual metaphor for the emotional weight of the scenario. The meme does not target any specific protected group but rather uses a universally recognized symbol of sadness (the dog) to amplify the perceived tragedy of the situation, which can be seen as insensitive and potentially offensive to those who have faced real-life financial or emotional hardship related to reproductive healthcare. The meme's intent is to shock and provoke laughter through the juxtaposition of a cute, sad animal with a dark, real-world scenario, which can be interpreted as a form of dark humor that may be considered inappropriate or offensive in certain contexts."@en .
