<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#backgroundPreserving> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Indicates one element placed only over neutral areas to preserve important content of another dimension.\nE.g. text placed only over neutral areas to preserve important visual content in memes"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01256#trivialization_of_medical_procedure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The act of making a serious medical or personal situation seem trivial or absurd through humor. The meme trivializes the serious and sensitive topic of abortion by linking it to a financial failure and an absurd consequence. This is a social trend and cultural phenomenon that helps explain the meme's intent and potential offensiveness."@en .
